BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:khoj-mozilla-counterstructures-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Khoj x Mozilla Foundation: Counterstructures Residency 20
 26 (Delhi)
DESCRIPTION:Counterstructures is Mozilla Foundation's cultural R&D residenc
 y\, in which creative technologists prototype alternatives to dominant tec
 h systems: cultural artifacts\, installations and tools that question and 
 reframe them. Each edition operationalises the findings of a regional part
 icipatory assembly into thematic tracks\; the Delhi edition\, hosted by Kh
 oj International Artists' Association\, works from Mozilla's assemblies wi
 th G5A in Delhi and Mumbai and runs on two tracks. RETAINING CULTURAL AUTH
 ORITY asks what happens when oral\, embodied or community-held knowledge i
 s converted into datasets and machine-readable forms\, which cultural mate
 rials become visible to AI systems and which do not\, and how communities 
 can retain authority over what is digitised\, interpreted\, reused or deli
 berately kept private. REMEMBERING AND THINKING WITH MACHINES asks where t
 hought resides when people think with machines\, at what stage human judgm
 ent enters the system\, and what cultural or professional knowledge is los
 t when judgment is standardised through automation. Proposals may respond 
 to one or both tracks and can take many forms\, but must critically counte
 r the questions the tracks raise rather than simply illustrate them. WHAT 
 RESIDENTS DO: prototype an artifact\, installation\, system\, artwork or t
 ool for public exhibition\; take part in listening\, reading\, workshops a
 nd facilitated critique\, testing ideas with peers and community members\;
  write a 750-word report on the project's development and insights for the
  Counterstructures report and online archive\; and present the work public
 ly. WHO IT IS FOR: creative technologists and multidisciplinary artists us
 ing technology as a medium for cultural inquiry\, bringing critical perspe
 ctives and research-driven practice. Experience with AI can be early-stage
  or advanced\, but SOME PROFICIENCY WITH CODING IS REQUIRED. ELIGIBILITY: 
 this Delhi edition is open to Indian nationals only. Earlier editions ran 
 with tiat in San Francisco (responding to Hollywood's 8 Rules for AI) and 
 with Rhizome in New York\, whose residents showed at the New Museum. APPLY
  through the Mozilla Foundation form at https://mozillafoundation.tfaforms
 .net/f/khojresidency\; the guiding principles for the call are set out in 
 the form. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Khoj International 
 Artists' Association in collaboration with Mozilla Foundation\nLocation: N
 ew Delhi\, India. Weekly in-person sessions at Khoj. INDIAN NATIONALS ONLY
 .\nAward: Mozilla's Creative Futures: Counterstructures programme publishe
 s USD 2\,500 per resident (USD 2\,000 stipend plus a USD 500 materials bud
 get)\, along with weekly in-person work sessions\, guest lectures from pra
 ctitioners across art\, technology and community design\, and publication 
 of the finished project in the collective documentation report. CAVEAT: ne
 ither the Khoj call page nor the Mozilla application form restates a figur
 e for this six-week Delhi edition\, and the published package covers the t
 en-week format\, so confirm the amount with Khoj before applying. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Six weeks\, 1 October to 12 November 2026\, running
  weekly in Delhi\, with final projects presented publicly 13 to 15 Novembe
 r 2026.\n\nMore: https://khojstudios.org/opportunity/open-call-counterstru
 ctures-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://khojstudios.org/opportunity/open-call-counterstructures-residen
 cy/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India. Weekly in-person sessions at Khoj. INDIAN NATIO
 NALS ONLY.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:peripheral-acts-edition-2-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Peripheral Acts Edition 2: Leaning Out (UAE balcony resid
 ency)
DESCRIPTION:Peripheral Acts is an experimental\, artist-led residency progr
 amme supporting artistic production alongside dialogue\, exchange and site
 -responsive experimentation\, rooted in everyday urban life in the UAE. Th
 e second edition\, Leaning Out\, takes residential balconies as its site: 
 suspended between private life and public view\, the balcony becomes a sta
 ge for negotiations between host and guest\, inhabitant and observer\, fra
 ming questions of privacy\, voyeurism\, belonging and ownership. STRUCTURE
 : three commissioned artists take part in two phases. Phase 1 is four in-p
 erson gatherings hosted by residency programmer Shazia Salam in Dubai and 
 Abu Dhabi (1\, 7\, 14 and 21 November 2026\, roughly two hours each\; atte
 ndance at all four is expected). Phase 2 is a one-month balcony takeover p
 er artist (January\, February or March 2027)\, during which each resident 
 also hosts one (semi-)public event sharing their practice and process. The
 re is no fixed formula for what can happen on the site\; interventions are
  shaped by its conditions\, permissions and chance encounters\, carefully 
 testing the possibilities and boundaries of informal public intervention i
 n the UAE. FUNDING: AED 1\,000 commission fee plus AED 1\,500 production b
 udget per artist. ELIGIBILITY: artists currently based in the UAE with eas
 y\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own or one belonging to
  a friend or family member). Questions: shaziasalam.92@gmail.com. APPLY vi
 a the Google Form. DEADLINE: 4 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Peripheral A
 cts\, conceptualised and hosted by Shazia Salam and Priyanka Mehra\nLocati
 on: Dubai and Abu Dhabi\, UAE. Open to artists currently based in the UAE 
 with easy\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own\, or a frie
 nd's or family member's).\nAward: AED 1\,000 artist commission fee plus AE
 D 1\,500 production budget per artist. Three artists commissioned. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Phase 1: four in-person gatherings in Dubai and Ab
 u Dhabi on 1\, 7\, 14 and 21 November 2026 (approx. 2 hours each). Phase 2
 : one-month balcony takeovers\, January\, February or March 2027 (one arti
 st per month).\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScVzoHsSO
 bapDUhXkeK02Ya1JpxzQH3QjVRtvhfoWDM-KWeSA/viewform?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScVzoHsSObapDUhXkeK02Ya1JpxzQH
 3QjVRtvhfoWDM-KWeSA/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Dubai and Abu Dhabi\, UAE. Open to artists currently based in the 
 UAE with easy\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own\, or a 
 friend's or family member's).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:making-space-guangzhou-nl-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Deadline: Making Space Residency 2027 for Netherlands-Based Practit
 ioners (Guangzhou)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in China\, in par
 tnership with artist-run space Making Space in Guangzhou\, invites Netherl
 ands-based artists\, makers\, curators\, writers\, researchers and other c
 ultural practitioners to a six-week residency in spring 2027. Making Space
  (est. 2017) focuses on art and social practice with an emphasis on long-t
 erm research\, local knowledge and care-driven collaboration. The residenc
 y is process-oriented with no obligation to produce finished work\; the re
 sident takes part in at least one public exchange (talk\, workshop\, readi
 ng group\, screening\, performance or open studio). SUPPORT: EUR 2\,700 tr
 avel and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives s
 hare the amount)\, accommodation in Guangzhou\, shared studio space\, cura
 torial and research support with access to local networks\, and logistical
  support for public programming (extra funding may be considered for publi
 c programmes). The resident arranges their own China visa\; Making Space p
 rovides an invitation letter. LOOKING FOR: practitioners engaging with alt
 ernative education\, ecological justice\, migration and labour\, social pr
 actice\, intergenerational narratives\, diaspora and transdisciplinary col
 laboration\; English communication required. APPLY by email (makingspace20
 17@gmail.com) with a 200-word bio\, CV\, 2-page project proposal and portf
 olio (max 20 pages) in a single PDF\, in English. Result expected late Nov
 ember 2026. Deadline: 3 October 2026\, 23:59 CST / 17:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Making Space\, in partnership with the Embassy of the Kingdom of the
  Netherlands in China\nLocation: Guangzhou\, China\nAward: EUR 2\,700 trav
 el and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives sha
 re it)\, plus accommodation in Guangzhou and shared studio space\nDuration
 : Six continuous weeks between 15 March and 15 June 2027\, dates agreed wi
 th the selected resident\n\nMore: https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Guangzhou\, China
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tokyo-biennale-2027-social-dive@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tokyo Biennale 2027: Social Dive open call
DESCRIPTION:Social Dive is the Tokyo Biennale 2027 open call for art projec
 ts and artist-in-residence proposals developed through research and engage
 ment with local communities across Tokyo. Participants immerse themselves 
 in the city's neighborhoods\, from temples and historic wooden buildings t
 o business districts\, train stations and shopping streets. Selected proje
 cts are developed at 11 designated sites: Toeizan Kaneiji Temple\, Yushima
  Seido\, Otemachi/Marunouchi/Yurakucho\, Kyobashi\, Nihonbashi\, Yaesu\, K
 anda\, Ueno Station\, Tokyo Dome City\, Akihabara Electric Town\, and Baku
 rocho/Higashi-Kanda. Proposals must respond to the biennale theme From Me 
 to Us and be presented during Tokyo Biennale 2027 (1 October to 11 Decembe
 r 2027). WHAT YOU GET: JPY 100\,000 honorarium\, round-trip travel up to J
 PY 300\,000\, accommodation in Tokyo\, project development support up to J
 PY 200\,000\, venue coordination\, interpretation and translation support\
 , and an invitation letter. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: artists\, curators\, research
 ers\, collectives and practitioners in related fields\, aged 18 or older\,
  from anywhere in the world\; must be available for on-site research\, col
 laboration and implementation in Tokyo with a residency of at least one mo
 nth including the opening\; one proposal per applicant. SELECTION: two-sta
 ge evaluation on theme responsiveness\, originality\, feasibility and comm
 unity collaboration. DEADLINE: 30 September 2026\, 23:59 JST. TO APPLY: vi
 a the online form with profile photo\, personal statement (150 words)\, tw
 o key visuals\, project summary and background\, detailed description (400
  words)\, budget breakdown and schedule\, and CV or portfolio (max 5 pages
 ). Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Tokyo Biennale\nLocation: Tokyo\, Japan
 \, at 11 designated sites. Open worldwide with no restrictions on national
 ity\, residence or base of operations\; requires on-site research and a re
 sidency of at least one month including the opening period.\nAward: JPY 10
 0\,000 honorarium (incl. tax)\, round-trip travel expenses up to JPY 300\,
 000 (economy\, one person)\, accommodation in Tokyo\, project development 
 support up to JPY 200\,000 (incl. tax)\, plus venue coordination\, interpr
 etation and translation support and an invitation letter. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Flexible residency (minimum one month including the opening
  period)\, with projects presented during Tokyo Biennale 2027\, 1 October 
 to 11 December 2027\n\nMore: https://socialdive.jp/en/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://socialdive.jp/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Tokyo\, Japan\, at 11 designated sites. Open worldwide with no res
 trictions on nationality\, residence or base of operations\; requires on-s
 ite research and a residency of at least one month including the opening p
 eriod.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi Museum: SIXI AiR Open Call 2027 Spring & Autumn (Nan
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:The Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project\, run by Six
 i Museum in Nanjing since 2024\, selects 4 artists across two three-month 
 sessions in 2027 (Spring\, March to May\, and Autumn\, September to Novemb
 er). The program is built as an open network across the city\, connecting 
 residents with local scholars\, artists\, historic neighborhoods and natur
 al landscapes\, with Open Studios and workshops along the way. Proposals m
 ust respond to one of two themes: Flux and Imprints\, Contemporary Echoes 
 of Migration History (cross-regional mobility\, cultural reconstruction an
 d memory\, including family histories of overseas Chinese\, the legacy of 
 colonialism in Asia\, and identity within global geopolitics)\, or Folds o
 f Text\, Cross-Media Intertextuality and Intervention (text as a fluid med
 ium\, with interdisciplinary work across literature\, linguistics\, music 
 and sound\, and visual arts). SUPPORT: round-trip flights\, visa fees\, in
 surance\, private apartment or loft studio\, material allowance\, technica
 l assistance\, airport pickup and translation\; no separate artist fee or 
 stipend is mentioned. ELIGIBILITY: artists of all disciplines\, aged 18 or
  older\, proficient in spoken and written Mandarin or English. HOW TO APPL
 Y: email a CV with profile photo\, portfolio and residency proposal as a s
 ingle PDF or ZIP with the subject line Residency Application. Final respon
 ses by mid-February 2027\; allow 2 to 3 months for visa processing. DEADLI
 NE: 15 November 2026 (GMT+8).\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: Nanj
 ing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural backgrounds\,
  aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.\nAward: Round-trip 
 flights\, visa application fees\, insurance\, and a private city-center ap
 artment or loft studio on the outskirts\, plus a material allowance (amoun
 t not published)\, technical assistance\, airport pickup and translation s
 upport. NO artist fee or stipend mentioned. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Three months: Spring 2027 (March to May) or Autumn 2027 (September to Nov
 ember).\n\nMore: https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural b
 ackgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sam-residencies-cycle-4-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: SAM Residencies Open Call: Cycle 4 (2027/2028) at Singapo
 re Art Museum
DESCRIPTION:The Singapore Art Museum's SAM Residencies programme\, hosted i
 n post-industrial warehouse spaces at Tanjong Pagar Distripark\, opens its
  fourth cycle for residencies between June 2027 and December 2028. Three t
 racks are available: Artist Residency (new artistic research\, experimenta
 tion and modes of making)\, Community & Education Residency (practice at t
 he intersection of art\, education and community engagement)\, and Curator
 ial & Research Residency (new approaches to exhibition making and curatori
 al practice). SUPPORT: a monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 and a shared studio
  or co-working space for all residents\; international residents also get 
 a return economy flight\, housing arrangement and visa assistance\, while 
 Singapore-based residents get an additional monthly local allowance of SGD
  250. Residents lead at least two public presentations or activations\, su
 ch as Residency Thursdays\, Open Studios or an In Conversation showcase. E
 LIGIBILITY: open globally to artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers 
 and creative practitioners\; individuals\, duos and collectives from all m
 ediums and disciplines\; applicants must be over 21. International applica
 nts may apply for one to three months\, Singapore-based applicants for up 
 to six months. HOW TO APPLY: via the SurveyMonkey Apply portal with a CV\,
  portfolio\, statement of interest (500-1\,000 words) and a recommendation
  letter submitted by the recommender. No application fee. Queries to resid
 encies@singaporeartmuseum.sg. DEADLINE: 30 September 2026 at 11:59 PM (GMT
 +8).\n\nOrganisation: Singapore Art Museum\nLocation: Tanjong Pagar Distri
 park\, Singapore. Open to artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers and
  creative practitioners from across the globe\; individuals\, duos and col
 lectives welcome.\nAward: Monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 plus a shared stud
 io or co-working space for all residents. International residents also rec
 eive a return economy flight\, housing arrangement and visa assistance\; S
 ingapore-based residents receive an additional monthly local allowance of 
 SGD 250. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency period June 2027 to Dece
 mber 2028\; international applicants may apply for one to three months\, S
 ingapore-based applicants for up to six months\n\nMore: https://www.singap
 oreartmuseum.sg/residencies/announcements/open-call-cycle-4?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.singaporeartmuseum.sg/residencies/announcements/open-call-c
 ycle-4?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tanjong Pagar Distripark\, Singapore. Open to artists\, curators\,
  educators\, researchers and creative practitioners from across the globe\
 ; individuals\, duos and collectives welcome.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
